From: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fan: do not log an error when pwmN_enable is absent

enablePwm() was added for I2C fan controllers such as the MAX31790, which
boot into an automatic regulation mode and must be switched to manual by
writing 1 to pwmN_enable before pwmN takes effect (commit abf91de1876,
"FanSensor: Add initial of pwm enable file").

Drivers whose PWM channels are always under direct control expose no
pwmN_enable attribute at all. aspeed-pwm-tacho is one of them -- it
registers only pwmN and fanN_input -- so on any AST2400/2500/2600 board
that drives its fans from the SoC, every configured PWM channel logs

    Error read/write '/sys/class/hwmon/hwmon0/pwmN_enable'

once per config reload, forever. Nothing is actually wrong: the PWM is
writable and the fan sensors come up normally, so the message is pure
noise that masks real fan faults in the journal.

Check for the file before opening it and return silently when it does not
exist, which is exactly how enableFanInput() immediately below already
handles a missing fanN_enable ("some drivers don't provide this file if
the sensors are always enabled"). A file that exists but cannot be opened
is still a genuine error and is still logged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
 src/fan/FanMain.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
index c6a8f57e8..8b20d20a5 100644
--- a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
+++ b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
@@ -122,8 +122,22 @@ FanTypes getFanType(const std::filesystem::path& parentPath)

     return FanTypes::i2c;
 }
+// The argument to this function should be the pwmN_enable file for the PWM
+// channel we are about to drive. Some drivers do not provide this file because
+// their PWM channels are always under direct (manual) control and have no
+// automatic regulation mode to switch out of -- aspeed-pwm-tacho, used by every
+// AST2400/2500/2600 BMC that drives fans from the SoC, is one of them. That is
+// not an error, so treat a missing file the same way enableFanInput() below
+// treats a missing fanN_enable: silently do nothing.
 void enablePwm(const std::filesystem::path& filePath)
 {
+    std::error_code ec;
+    bool exists = std::filesystem::exists(filePath, ec);
+    if (ec || !exists)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+
     std::fstream enableFile(filePath, std::ios::in | std::ios::out);
     if (!enableFile.good())
     {
